    {
      "id": "claim_132a1d96814d4720bb835685696aee7a",
      "statement": "The init flow calls pki.New, prompts for a password (provisioner-only in RA mode; CA keys plus first provisioner for standalone unless --provisioner-password-file splits them), generates provisioner key pairs for standalone only, generates the root certificate (or copies an existing --root cert without copying its key into STEPPATH) and always the intermediate, optionally generates SSH signing keys, and ends with p.WriteHelmTemplate(os.Stdout) for --helm or p.Save() otherwise.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/init.go#L649-L717",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:35f71ef6e39aaaaf5b2fc5f531863b94a8012a9068e0260fe473be4ef76d669c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_555611911ede4ee6a332c74de1aa05d8",
      "statement": "OfflineCA is a process-wide singleton because double initialization is sometimes not possible due to locks (as seen in badgerDB): the first NewOfflineCA call wins for the whole process, only one ca-config can be used per invocation, while separate step subprocesses are unaffected.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/offline.go#L36-L81",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:535a7ad7ebf3f401a29b0c771c81fe1d6113871042646acb5be94508de7544d1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3e4fbd76431546f8b0fb67370c9f8386",
      "statement": "OfflineCA derives its identity from ca.json: GetCaURL/CaURL are https://<first DNS name> with IPv6 bracketed by toHostname, Audience(tokType) mirrors the online audiences (/sign, /renew, /revoke, /ssh/sign, /ssh/renew, /ssh/rekey), GetRootCAs returns nil, and the provisioner list comes from config.AuthorityConfig.Provisioners which must be non-empty.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://utils/cautils/offline.go#L83-L173",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:90536af4871aa9210ce9da0256cd4ae589b895481d1885a27e60cc9cbd7586aa:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_da0f12351c294b379800af6481d8cdd2",
      "statement": "OfflineCA.Renew/Revoke/Rekey recover the presenting client certificate from the http.RoundTripper's TLSClientConfig.Certificates[0] (documented as internal code that should not panic), because commands such as newRenewer build a real http.Transport carrying the client certificate and pass that same transport to the offline client; Renew falls back to the x5c token path when --mtls is off or the certificate is expired.",
      "evidence": [
